<title>AUSTRALIA: Foster's sees no Molson talks impact.</title>
<headline>Foster's sees no Molson talks impact.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foster's Brewing Group Ltd said on Monday it did not expect the outcome of the dispute involving its 40 percent owned Molson Breweries with Coors Brewing Co to have a severe impact on the group's bottom line</p>
<p>&quot;I don't expect it to have any severe impact, if you like, on the abnormals,&quot; Foster's chief executive Ted Kunkel told reporters after the brewer released its half year result.</p>
<p>Molson and Coor's were discussing a new licensing deal after a court ruling terminated their previous arrangement under which Molsen brewed and marketed Coors beer brands in Canada.</p>
</text>
